I left out the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0`, so it has no HTTP import, and sending the tick's text to an external host would also leak input data outside the graph. The output otherwise stays the same. The code below reads the clock and returns the date and start time.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{tick, run-info};

    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(tick: tick) -> run-info;
}
```

